[TITLE:e200 Cores Manual Validation Plan - Certification Improvements]

[INTRO]
This document provides a validation plan to verify LLVM e200 core implementation
against the official reference manuals. Manuals are now available:
- e200z0: https://www.elektronikjk.com/elementy_czynne/IC/E200Z0.pdf
- e200z4: https://www.elektronikjk.com/elementy_czynne/IC/E200Z4.pdf

[MANUAL-STATUS]
UID: MANUAL-STATUS
STATUS: Available

e200z0_CORE_REFERENCE_MANUAL:
- URL: https://www.elektronikjk.com/elementy_czynne/IC/E200Z0.pdf
- Document: e200z0 Power Architecture™ Core Reference Manual
- Document Number: E200Z0CRM
- Revision: Rev. 0, 4/2008
- Publisher: Freescale Semiconductor (now NXP)

e200z4_CORE_REFERENCE_MANUAL:
- URL: https://www.elektronikjk.com/elementy_czynne/IC/E200Z4.pdf
- Document: e200z4 Power Architecture™ Core Reference Manual
- Document Number: e200z4RM
- Revision: Rev. 0, 10/2009
- Publisher: Freescale Semiconductor (now NXP)

[VALIDATION-CERT-001]
UID: VAL-001
TITLE: Validate e200z0 Pipeline Scheduling Model (CERT-001)

MANUAL_SECTIONS:
- Chapter 4: Instruction Pipeline and Execution Timing
- Section 4.1: Pipeline Overview
- Section 4.2: Instruction Timing
- Section 4.3: Execution Timing Tables

VALIDATION_CHECKLIST:
1. Verify 4-stage pipeline model:
   - [ ] Confirm IF (Instruction Fetch) stage
   - [ ] Confirm ID (Instruction Decode) stage
   - [ ] Confirm EX (Execute) stage
   - [ ] Confirm WB (Write Back) stage
   - [ ] Verify NO separate MEM stage (memory in EX)

2. Verify instruction latencies:
   - [ ] Integer simple operations: Verify 1 cycle latency
   - [ ] Integer compare operations: Verify 1-2 cycle latency
   - [ ] Multiply operations: Verify 4 cycle latency
   - [ ] Divide operations: Verify 34 cycle latency
   - [ ] Load operations: Verify 3 cycle latency (FETCH+DECODE+EX+WB)
   - [ ] Store operations: Verify 3 cycle latency
   - [ ] Branch operations: Verify 1 cycle latency
   - [ ] SPR operations (MFSPR/MTSPR): Verify 1 cycle latency

3. Verify bypass paths:
   - [ ] GPR bypass: Verify EX to EX forwarding latency
   - [ ] CR bypass: Verify condition register forwarding
   - [ ] Document any additional bypass paths

4. Verify functional units:
   - [ ] ALU (Integer ALU)
   - [ ] BU (Branch Unit)
   - [ ] LSU (Load/Store Unit)
   - [ ] MUL (Multiply Unit)
   - [ ] Verify resource sharing constraints

5. Verify branch misprediction penalty:
   - [ ] Current model: 3 cycles
   - [ ] Verify against manual specification

6. Verify load-to-use latency:
   - [ ] Current model: 4 cycles (3 cycles + 1 writeback)
   - [ ] Verify against manual specification

CODE_LOCATIONS_TO_VERIFY:
- llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCScheduleE200Z0.td:48-201 (itineraries)
- llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCScheduleE200Z0.td:218-230 (model parameters)

[VALIDATION-CERT-003]
UID: VAL-003
TITLE: Validate Interrupt Handler Context Save (CERT-003)

MANUAL_SECTIONS:
- Chapter 5: Interrupts and Exceptions
- Section 5.1: Exception Model Overview
- Section 5.2: Exception Types
- Section 5.3: Exception Handling
- Section 5.4: Returning from Exception Handler
- Chapter 2: Register Model
- Section 2.3: Special Purpose Register Descriptions
- Section 2.4.3: Special Purpose Register Summary

VALIDATION_CHECKLIST:
1. Verify interrupt return mechanism:
   - [ ] RFI instruction: Verify correct usage (BookE requirement)
   - [ ] e_rfi instruction: Verify VLE mode requirement
   - [ ] Link register (LR): Verify save/restore requirements
   - [ ] Status registers (SRR0/SRR1): Verify automatic save/restore

2. Verify interrupt context save requirements:
   - [ ] GPR (General Purpose Registers): Verify save requirements
   - [ ] CR (Condition Register): Verify save requirements
   - [ ] LR (Link Register): Verify save requirements
   - [ ] SPR (Special Purpose Registers): Identify which must be saved
   - [ ] FPR (Floating-Point Registers): N/A for e200z0 (no FPU)
   - [ ] FPSCR: N/A for e200z0 (no FPU)

3. Verify IVOR (Interrupt Vector Offset Register) table:
   - [ ] Critical interrupt: IVOR0 specification
   - [ ] External interrupt: IVOR4 specification
   - [ ] Other interrupt types and IVOR mappings
   - [ ] Differentiate context save requirements by interrupt type

4. Verify exception handling:
   - [ ] Exception entry sequence
   - [ ] Exception exit sequence (RFI)
   - [ ] MSR (Machine State Register) handling
   - [ ] Context synchronization requirements

CODE_LOCATIONS_TO_VERIFY:
- llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCFrameLowering.cpp:1843-1913 (interrupt context save)
- llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCFrameLowering.cpp:1662-1686 (RFI/e_rfi handling)

[VALIDATION-CERT-005]
UID: VAL-005
TITLE: Validate Exception Handling (CERT-005)

MANUAL_SECTIONS:
- Chapter 5: Interrupts and Exceptions
- Section 5.2: Exception Types
- Section 5.2.X: Program Exceptions
- Section 5.2.X: Arithmetic Exceptions
- Chapter 3: Instruction Model
- Section 3.X: Division Instructions

VALIDATION_CHECKLIST:
1. Verify division exception behavior:
   - [ ] Division by zero: Hardware trap or software check required?
   - [ ] Exception type: Program exception or system exception?
   - [ ] Exception latency: Cycles from division to exception
   - [ ] XER register: Overflow bit handling

2. Verify integer overflow:
   - [ ] Overflow detection mechanism
   - [ ] Exception generation for overflow
   - [ ] XER register: SO (Summary Overflow) bit behavior

3. Verify exception handler requirements:
   - [ ] Exception handler entry point
   - [ ] Register state at exception entry
   - [ ] Exception handler return sequence

CODE_LOCATIONS_TO_VERIFY:
- llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCScheduleE200Z0.td:81-86 (division latency)
- llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCISelLowering.cpp (exception lowering)

[VALIDATION-CERT-006]
UID: VAL-006
TITLE: Validate Memory Barrier Semantics (CERT-006)

MANUAL_SECTIONS:
- Chapter 3: Instruction Model
- Section 3.4: Memory Synchronization and Reservation Instructions
- Chapter 4: Instruction Pipeline and Execution Timing
- Memory access timing specifications

VALIDATION_CHECKLIST:
1. Verify memory barrier instructions:
   - [ ] MSYNC: Verify exact semantics for BookE
   - [ ] SYNC: Verify if supported (or MSYNC only)
   - [ ] LWSYNC: Verify if supported
   - [ ] ISYNC: Verify instruction synchronization

2. Verify memory ordering:
   - [ ] Store-before-load ordering guarantees
   - [ ] Memory barrier latency
   - [ ] Cache coherency requirements (if cache exists)

3. Verify reservation instructions:
   - [ ] LWARX (load word and reserve indexed)
   - [ ] STWCX (store word conditional indexed)
   - [ ] Reservation granule size

CODE_LOCATIONS_TO_VERIFY:
- llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCInstrInfo.td:2341-2358 (MSYNC/SYNC definitions)
- llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCISelLowering.cpp (memory barrier lowering)

[VALIDATION-CERT-010]
UID: VAL-010
TITLE: Validate Register Spill/Fill Timing (CERT-010)

MANUAL_SECTIONS:
- Chapter 4: Instruction Pipeline and Execution Timing
- Load/store instruction timing
- Stack pointer operations

VALIDATION_CHECKLIST:
1. Verify stack access timing:
   - [ ] Store to stack (STW): Verify latency
   - [ ] Load from stack (LWZ): Verify latency
   - [ ] Stack pointer update: Verify latency
   - [ ] Cache behavior: Verify if stack accesses are cached

2. Verify register save/restore:
   - [ ] Multiple register save (STMW): Verify if supported
   - [ ] Multiple register load (LMW): Verify if supported
   - [ ] Register save/restore latency in interrupt context

CODE_LOCATIONS_TO_VERIFY:
- llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCInstrInfo.cpp:1095-1118 (spill operations)
- llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCInstrInfo.cpp:1157-1176 (fill operations)

[VALIDATION-CERT-004]
UID: VAL-004
TITLE: Validate VLE Register Constraints (CERT-004) - e200z4 Manual

MANUAL_SECTIONS:
- e200z4 Core Reference Manual: VLE specification
- Chapter 3: Instruction Model
- VLE encoding rules

VALIDATION_CHECKLIST:
1. Verify VLE register constraints:
   - [ ] 16-bit instructions: Verify R0-R7 requirement (3-bit encoding)
   - [ ] 32-bit instructions: Verify R0-R31 support
   - [ ] Instruction selection rules: When to use 16-bit vs 32-bit

2. Verify immediate value constraints:
   - [ ] s6imm: Verify -32 to 31 range
   - [ ] u5imm: Verify 0 to 31 range
   - [ ] u7imm: Verify 0 to 127 range
   - [ ] u4imm: Verify 0 to 15 range
   - [ ] Boundary value handling

CODE_LOCATIONS_TO_VERIFY:
- llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCInstrVLE.td:22-70 (immediate predicates)
- llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCRegisterInfo.td:327 (GPRC_VLE_R0_R7 register class)

[EXTRACTION-PRIORITY]
UID: EXTRACT-PRIORITY

HIGH_PRIORITY_EXTRACTION:
1. e200z0 Chapter 4: Instruction Pipeline and Execution Timing
   - Complete instruction latency tables
   - Pipeline stage breakdown
   - Bypass path specifications
   - Load-to-use latency

2. e200z0 Chapter 5: Interrupts and Exceptions
   - IVOR table
   - Exception entry/exit sequences
   - Register save requirements
   - RFI instruction semantics

3. e200z0 Chapter 3: Instruction Model
   - Division instruction behavior
   - Memory barrier semantics
   - Exception specifications

MEDIUM_PRIORITY_EXTRACTION:
1. e200z4 Manual: VLE specification sections
2. e200z4 Manual: Dual-issue pairing rules
3. e200z4 Manual: SPE/FPU instruction timing

[VALIDATION-PROCESS]
UID: VAL-PROCESS

STEP_1_EXTRACT:
Extract key information from manuals:
1. Create spreadsheet/table with instruction latencies from Chapter 4
2. Extract IVOR table from Chapter 5
3. Extract exception specifications from Chapter 5
4. Extract memory barrier semantics from Chapter 3

STEP_2_COMPARE:
Compare extracted data with LLVM implementation:
1. Instruction latencies: Compare manual vs PPCScheduleE200Z0.td
2. Pipeline stages: Verify stage structure matches manual
3. Interrupt handling: Compare manual vs PPCFrameLowering.cpp
4. Exception handling: Verify manual requirements vs implementation

STEP_3_DOCUMENT_DISCREPANCIES:
Document any differences:
1. Create discrepancy report
2. Prioritize by certification impact
3. Propose fixes for each discrepancy

STEP_4_IMPLEMENT_FIXES:
Implement fixes based on manual specifications:
1. Update instruction latencies if incorrect
2. Fix interrupt context save logic
3. Implement missing exception handling
4. Correct memory barrier usage

STEP_5_VERIFY:
Verify fixes against manual:
1. Re-run validation checklist
2. Update CompleteModel flags if appropriate
3. Create regression tests based on manual specs

[MANUAL-CHAPTER-MAPPING]
UID: MANUAL-MAP

e200z0_MANUAL_STRUCTURE:
Chapter 1: e200z0 and e200z0h Overview
Chapter 2: Register Model → CERT-003 (interrupt context save)
Chapter 3: Instruction Model → CERT-005 (exceptions), CERT-006 (memory barriers)
Chapter 4: Instruction Pipeline and Execution Timing → CERT-001 (scheduling), CERT-010 (spill timing)
Chapter 5: Interrupts and Exceptions → CERT-003 (interrupt handling), CERT-005 (exceptions)
Chapter 6: Core Complex Interfaces
Chapter 7: Power Management
Chapter 8: Debug Support
Chapter 9: Nexus 2+ Module

